N2  - The proceedings contain 45 papers. The topics discussed include: collaborating with cardiac services when treating parturients with complex cardiac disease. creating a standard of practice; impact of pregnancy-related acute kidney injury on maternal and fetal outcomes in high dependency unit admissions in the United Kingdom; management of the pregnant and post-partum patient on the acute medical ward: a retrospective audit; national time trends in preeclampsia and gestational diabetes in Denmark and Canada, 2005-2018 - a path towards poorer cardiometabolic health?; patient perspectives on lifestyle intervention programs after hypertensive disorders of pregnancy: a qualitative study; a case of spontaneous hemoperitoneum in pregnancy; a congenital conundrum: chondrodysplasia punctata in maternal mixed connective tissue disease; and successful management of idiopathic granulomatous mastitis in pregnancy and lactation with prednisone and azathioprine.
