N2  - Introduction: Diabetes mellitus is a disorder of carbohydrate metabolism0 It is most common medical complication of pregnancy0 Women can be separated into those who were known to have diabetes before pregnancy-pregestational or overt, and those diagnosed before pregnancy- gestational diabetes0 Gestational diabetes mellitus (GDM) is defined as any degree of glucose intolerance with onset or first recognition during pregnancy 10 Pregnancy confers a state of insulin resistance and hyperinsulinemia that may predispose some women to develop diabetes0 Gestational diabetes mellitus (GDM) occurs when a woman’s pancreatic function is not sufficient to overcome the diabetogenic environment of pregnancy0 Undiagnosed or inadequately treated GDM can lead to significant maternal & fetal complications 20 Aims and Objectives Feto-maternal outcome in patients of pregnancy with diabetes was studied with following aims * To review different diagnostic criteria for GDM0 * To study proportion of diabetes in pregnancy, both gestational diabetes and overt diabetes0 * To study feto-maternal outcome and complication in pregnancy with diabetes0 * To plan management of pregnancy with diabetes and to decrease fetomaternal morbidity and mortality0 Materials and Methods A prospective case study was conducted on 70 Diabetic Patients at a tertiary care centre ND Desai Institute of Medical science and research, Nadiad, to study the fetomaternal outcome during December 2020 to August 20210 All necessary investigations were carried out0 The data collected was analyzed and tabulations were made0 Result and Discussion Total 70 patients were analyzed0 Out of them maximum patients had gestational diabetes rather than Overt diabetes0 maximum patients belonged to age group 20-29 years0 maximum patients had positive family history of diabetes and were multipara with polyhydroamnios0 Maximum patients required insulin for treatment of diabetes mellitus during pregnancy along with medical nutrition therapy and exercise0 Regular insulin was used in all patients0 maximum patients were delivered by caesarean section0.
