N2  - The proceedings contain 151 papers. The topics discussed include: making the most of exome sequencing data from family trios with probands affected by very rare birth defects; the genotype by environment interaction (G×E) in inbred lines and hybrids of maize; addressing the missing data issue in multi-phenotype genome-wide association studies; genetic architecture of gene expression traits across diverse populations; genetics of the measure of physiological dysregulation: findings from the health and retirement study; efficient fine-mapping to identify causal genetic variants and quantify their contribution to complex phenotypes; maternal and fetal genetic effects on birth weight and their relevance to cardio-metabolic disease; persistent organochlorine pollutants: genetic variations associated with p,p'-DDE and PCB153 blood levels among women in france; bivariate genome-wide association study reveals new variants associated with eosinophil cationic protein and eosinophil-derived neurotoxin levels; should cases with a clinical diagnosis of giant cell arteritis be included in genetic association studies? analysis of the UK giant cell arteritis consortium cohort; phenome-wide investigation of Alzheimer's disease-related phenotypes; prediction of treatment response from genome-wide SNP data in rheumatoid arthritis patients; trans-ethnic meta-analysis of gestational diabetes reveals shared genetic background with type 2 diabetes; and evaluation of a targeted custom capture bisulfite sequencing approach.
