N2  - From the early stages of pregnancy until birth, the interface between mother and child is the umbilical cord. The available knowledge regarding this so important organ for the continuance of life during pregnancy, is quite limited. The umbilical cord may appear a number of anatomical and mechanical abnormalities. These abnormalities may cause suspicious or abnormal cardiotocographic patterns during pregnancy and labour. The presence of variable decelerations during pregnancy or labor is quite common in umbilical cord abnormalities.
