N2  - The proceedings contain 100 papers. The topics discussed include: a cross-sectional, multi-centric, epidemiological study of diabetic neuropathy and associated co-morbidities in type 2 diabetic patients in India; triple oral fixed dose combination of glimepiride, metformin and low dose (7.5 mg) pioglitazone in the treatment of uncontrolled type 2 diabetes; safety, feasibility and short term complication following lsagb (laparoscopic single anastomosis gastric bypass), results in the first 277 cases; lipoprotein(a) serum levels and its relationship to the severity of retinopathy in type 2 diabetes mellitus; association of serum ferritin with insulin resistance in offsprings of type 2 diabetes mellitus; relation of mean platelet volume with serum paraoxonase-1 activity and in diabetic patients with respect to obesity and diabetic complications; effects of l-carnitine in sodium nitroprusside (SNP) induced raw 264.7 macrophages; gene polymorphism in essential hypertension & its relation to environmental factors in north Indians; association of hypertriglyceridaemia with gestational diabetes and adverse pregnancy outcomes; cs6253 abca1 agonist treatment of apoe4 driven Alzheimers's disease; predicting 10-year risk of diabetes incidence in middle-aged and elderly: the BLSA study; the role of uric acid in impairment of the glomerular filteration rate in nonproteinuric patients with type 2 diabetes mellitus; systemic levels of angiogenesis and angiostasis CXC chemokines are differed in neonates delivered mothers suffering gestational diabetes mellitus and their neonates; and NT-PROBNP levels can predict heart dysfunction in diabetic senescent patients.
