N2  - This paper presents a 26 year old primigravid with a chief complaint of leg swelling on her 26 weeks AOG. Dupplex scan of the left lower extremity was done and revealed subacute venous thrombosis and venous insufficiency of the right leg. On routine prenatal check up, patient was diagnosed with Gestational Diabetes Mellitus, hence intervention with medical nutrition therapy was advised. Multi- specialty referral to Cardiology, Hematology and Surgery was done to manage both medical and obstetrical concerns of the patient. On her 30 weeks AOG, she was admitted for preterm labor and was started on tocolysis with magnesium sulfate. Thereafter anti-coagulation with heparin and unfractionated heparin was maintained until 37 weeks to prevent venous thromboembolism. Antenatal corticosteroids Dexamethasone was administered at 34 weeks for fetal lung maturity. Weekly antenatal surveillance with Biophysical Scoring, Non Stress Test, and fetal movement counting was accomplished as recommended by perinatology service. At 38 weeks and 2 days, patient had spontaneous onset of labor and eventually delivered vaginally under epidural anesthesia. She delivered to a live baby boy with Apgar score of 7,9 Birthweight of 2948 grams. Effective post partum family planning of choice with Depo Medroxy Progesterone Acetate was initiated at 6 weeks postpartum.
