N2  - The proceedings contain 255 papers. The topics discussed include: association between newly diagnosed diabetes and dementia diagnosis in older adults: a population-based study; interaction between maternal obesity and gestational diabetes mellitus and long-term development of diabetes, hypertension and cardiovascular disease: a population-level analysis; physical activity intensity and adiposity in obese youth: the POWER trial; inhibition of insulin-stimulated glucose transport by amino acids in muscle cells is not unique to leucine; a population-based study of diabetes incidence by ethnicity and age: support for the development of ethnic-specific screening and prevention strategies; weight loss intervention for individuals with diabetes and serious mental illness: a pragmatic experiment in community settings; assessing the impact of diabetes education: an observational study; and the effects of a community-based lifestyle intervention, PREPARE, on the physical activity levels of newly diagnosed persons with prediabetes: preliminary findings.
