N2  - The proceedings contain 700 papers. The topics discussed include: tight calorie control (TICACOS) in geriatric hip fracture patients; insulin therapy can inhibit the boosting effect on systemic inflammatory response due to overfeeding-induced hyperglycemia under septic conditions, resulting in nutritional stress; effect of prepregnancy obesity on fatty acids and birth outcomes in subjects with gestational diabetes mellitus; glutamine supplementation alleviates vasculopathy and alters plasma metabolome in an in vivo model of endothelial cell dysfunction; the impact of implementation of enteral feeding protocol on the improvement in enteral feeding practice of adult critically ill patients; standardized parenteral nutrition support in obese critically-ill patients; nutritional status and body composition of patients with typical geriatric bone fractures; and enteral tube feeding that includes EPA and DHA improves inflammation and iron metabolism in the elderly.
