N2  - Pregnancy associated with Diabetes Mellitus (DM) represents still a challenge for the obstetrician. Even if the maternal control of glicemia and the surveillance of the fetal status have been much improved, the fetus is at an elevated risk for congenital malformations. The fetal heart is influenced in her structure and function from the embryonic development and during the second and the third trimester. The fetal echocardiography must be used in all diabetic pregnancies for the detection of congenital heart disease (CHD) and of hypertrophic cardiomyopathy, thus improving the fetal prognosis.
