N2  - In summary, the reviews on the topics included in this issue describe the general to the specific mechanisms known on a particular membrane transport process that when altered is directly or indirectly associated with a pathology or contributes to pathological states such as tumor growth or altered fetal growth. This concept is proposed in this issue as 'transportalopathy' intending to join together the relationship between deficient (pathological) membrane transport systems and cell dysfunction. It is in fact vital to understand these and other mechanisms in detail to reach a level of knowledge where therapeutic decisions could be taken on the bases of fundamental research (i.e. basic science).
