N2  - Described as a myeloproliferative disorder mainly affecting elderly women, recent reports now confirm the occurrence of essential thrombocythemia at younger ages, which questions treatment during pregnancy. We report a further case of uneventful full term pregnancy with the use of interferon-α for maternal essential thrombocythemia which suggests that interferon-α could be considered as an effective and safe treatment during pregnancy for women with essential thrombocythemia. Further studies are warranted to determine whether interferon-α is the optimal therapeutic option during pregnancy for this patient population. Copyright © 2009 S. Karger AG.
