N2  - The aim of our work in the Clinic for Children Born by Women with Diabetes Mellitus and of this study is analysis of somatic and psychomotor development, diagnosis of possible carbohydrate and lipid metabolism disorders and congenital defects not diagnosed in early stage of medical care. 69 patients aged 1 month-13 years (38 children below 1 year) born by mothers with IDDM (32), NIDDM (7) and GDM (30) were included in the study. 20 children were born before 38 hbd, 39 by caesarean section. The health condition was established by medical examination, parents' interview and medical record. During medical examination physical development and neurological status with neurophysiological development of psychomotoric abilities by Vojta was of special attention. Laboratory tests included: blood test and glucose concentration in blood, aminotransferase level, urea test, fructosamine and glycosylated haemoglobin concentration, total cholesterol, HDL concentration and biochemical liver function tests. Immunological tests included: IgA, IgM, IgG, IgE and complement and immunological complexes level. Oxidative stress was evaluated by dimalonealdehyde level, vit. E concentration, peroxidative dismutase, glutathione peroxidase and total antioxidants level. We found a high percentage of high body weight at birth (over 97th percentile) in 30% of patients in relation to hbd. 6 children had neurological disorders (underwent observation for infantile cerebral palsy). 2.9% children had organic heart disease. Diabetes mellitus was diagnosed in 2 children (2.9%). A surprisingly high percentage of children had lipid metabolism and immunologic disorders. Considerable percentage of children had increased IgE levels and antibodies against bovine milk proteins (IgE).
