N2  - Excellent blood glucose control is necessary to reduce the excess fetal morbidity and mortality associated with the diabetic pregnancy. This article outlines the roles of glucose monitoring and insulin therapy in intensive treatment regimens during gestation. The discussion includes recommended monitoring frequency, glycemic standards, types of insulin and mechanism of action, goals and timing of insulin therapy, as well as the complications of insulin therapy.
