N2  - The hemodynamics was studied in 42 newborns with diabetic fetal diseases. Clinical and instrumental examinations revealed cardiomyopathy in 28 of these. Hemodynamic disorders were characterized by a low stroke volume resultant from reduced diastolic volume of the left ventricle. The most grave hemodynamic disorders! were detected in patients with the obstructive cardiomyopathy when both diastolic and systolic volumes of the left ventricle were changed, myocardia contractility reduced, and diastolic function suppressed.
